  "Number": 4,
  "Question": "Define the operation “\\(\\circ\\)” by \\(x\\circ y=4x-3y+xy,\\) for all real numbers \\(x\\) and \\(y.\\) For how many real numbers \\(y\\) does \\(3\\circ y=12?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(0\\)",
    "B": "\\(1\\)",
    "C": "\\(3\\)",
    "D": "\\(4\\)",
    "E": "more than \\(4\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "Substituting \\(x=3\\) makes the product term \\(3y\\), which cancels the subtracted \\(3y\\):\n\\[\n3\\circ y=4(3)-3y+3y=12.\n\\]\nThis equality holds for every real number \\(y\\), so every real number satisfies the equation. There are infinitely many solutions, hence more than \\(4\\). The answer is choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{E}}\\).",
